.TH WIFI 8 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
wifi \- connect to Wi\-Fi in one command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wifi scan
.br
.B wifi connect
.I SSID
.RI [ PASSWORD ]
.br
.BR "wifi up" " | " "wifi down" " | " "wifi status" " | " "wifi list"
.br
.B wifi forget
.I SSID
.br
.BR "wifi fallback" " | " "wifi static"
.I ADDRESS/PREFIX GATEWAY
.RI [ DNS ...]
.br
.B wifi dhcp
.br
.B wifi auto
.BR on | off
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wifi
does the usual
.BR wpa_supplicant ,
.B udhcpc
and
.B ip
steps for you, and prints each command it runs on a line starting with
.BR + ,
so you can see and learn exactly what happens.
It waits for the network to accept the password before asking for an
address, which is what makes it work on the first try.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Nearby networks, strongest first.
.TP
.BI connect " SSID " \fR[\fIPASSWORD\fR]
Save the network (the password is asked for if not given, and stored
hashed) and connect. An empty password means an open network.
.TP
.B up
Connect to the saved networks.
.TP
.B down
Disconnect.
.TP
.B status
Link, address and routes.
.TP
.B list
Saved networks.
.TP
.BI forget " SSID"
Remove a saved network.
.TP
.BI fallback " ADDRESS/PREFIX GATEWAY " \fR[\fIDNS ...\fR]
Try DHCP first; if it gives no address within about 30 seconds, use this
fixed address. DNS servers default to 1.1.1.1 and 9.9.9.9.
.TP
.BI static " ADDRESS/PREFIX GATEWAY " \fR[\fIDNS ...\fR]
Always use this fixed address, never DHCP.
.TP
.B dhcp
Forget the fixed address and use DHCP only.
.TP
.BR auto " on|off"
Connect at every boot. Same as
.BR "nni set WIFI_AUTO yes" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WIFI_IF
Use this wireless interface instead of the first one found.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
Saved networks.
.TP
.I /etc/nni/wifi\-static
The fixed\-address settings of
.BR fallback " and " static .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wifi scan
wifi connect "Home Network"
wifi fallback 192.168.1.50/24 192.168.1.1 1.1.1.1
wifi auto on
.fi
.SH NOTES
The minimal YnniOS edition needs
.B pol install wpasupplicant iw
and the firmware package for the Wi\-Fi card first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nni (8),
.BR nni.conf (5),
.BR wpa_supplicant (8),
.BR ip (8)
